### Lot 5 step 5a demo, till deposits, free places and the CRM export (IntelliJ HTTP client): plan lot-5 §13.1 Exit 5a
### (1)-(6), (8) on one instance; Lot5CashCrmFlowTest runs the same flow in CI.
#
# Start the backend with the dev profile on port 8080, so @base and the card redirect (PUBLIC_BASE_URL, dev default
# http://localhost:8080/v1) agree (dev seed: ATLAS FC with a cash point, Admin Dev +212600000001, Caissier Dev
# +212600000002, Ops Dev +212600000003, Finance Dev +212600000004, Grand Stade with Est and Sud; the simulated card
# gateway is on):
#   docker compose up -d && SERVER_PORT=8080 SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=dev ./gradlew bootRun
# Every phone logs in with the dev OTP 123456 (JOMHOR_DEV_FIXED_OTP, dev default). The fan phones are made up.
# Card payments: open the response's redirect_url in a browser and click "Approuver" right away (8 min hold).
# The two tills: Caissier Dev runs "Guichet Nord", Ops Dev "Guichet Sud" (one open till per staff member). A till left
# open by an earlier run answers 200 with it at 3.1/3.6: close it first. Each run makes a new match.
# Pass tickets (free.passes, step 5) come from lot5-passes.http: run it first with this match in its series to see
# them; without it free.passes reads 0. Karim's paid cotisation and Nadia's pass (step 6) come from the same file.
# At the end, backend/loadtest/check.sql must print no rows:
#   docker compose exec -T postgres psql -U jomhor -d jomhor < loadtest/check.sql

@base = http://localhost:8080/v1
@org = a7a5fc00-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
@venue = a7a5fc00-0000-4000-8000-000000000301
@adminPhone = +212600000001
@cashierPhone = +212600000002
@opsPhone = +212600000003
@financePhone = +212600000004
@buyerPhone = +212611177001
@yazidPhone = +212611177002
@karimPhone = +212611177003
@aminePhone = +212611177004
@saraPhone = +212611177005
@code = 123456
# Today, in the venue's zone (Africa/Casablanca): the deposits' slip date and the report ranges. Set it before a run.
@today = 2026-11-17

### ---------- (0) staff logins ----------

### 0.1 OPS (Ops Dev, also "Guichet Sud"): ask for a code
POST {{base}}/org/auth/otp
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{opsPhone}}"}

### 0.2 OPS: verify
POST {{base}}/org/auth/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{opsPhone}}", "code": "{{code}}"}

> {% client.global.set("orgToken", response.body.token); %}

### 0.3 ADMIN (Admin Dev): ask for a code (void, CRM export)
POST {{base}}/org/auth/otp
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{adminPhone}}"}

### 0.4 ADMIN: verify
POST {{base}}/org/auth/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{adminPhone}}", "code": "{{code}}"}

> {% client.global.set("adminToken", response.body.token); %}

### 0.5 CASHIER (Caissier Dev, "Guichet Nord"): ask for a code
POST {{base}}/org/auth/otp
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{cashierPhone}}"}

### 0.6 CASHIER: verify
POST {{base}}/org/auth/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{cashierPhone}}", "code": "{{code}}"}

> {% client.global.set("cashierToken", response.body.token); %}

### 0.7 FINANCE (Finance Dev): ask for a code
POST {{base}}/org/auth/otp
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{financePhone}}"}

### 0.8 FINANCE: verify
POST {{base}}/org/auth/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{financePhone}}", "code": "{{code}}"}

> {% client.global.set("financeToken", response.body.token); %}

### ---------- (1) Set-up: the match, "Plein tarif" 150 DH, "Tribune" 250 DH, "Presse" (Invitations) ----------

### 1.1 OPS: the Grand Stade zones (Est)
GET {{base}}/org/venues/{{venue}}
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

> {% client.global.set("estId", response.body.zones.find(z => z.code === "EST").id); %}

### 1.2 OPS: the match (DRAFT)
POST {{base}}/org/events
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"venue_id": "{{venue}}", "event_type": "FOOTBALL_MATCH", "title": "ATLAS FC – Démo dépôts",
 "starts_at": "2027-01-31T19:00:00Z", "metadata": {"opponent": "Démo"}}

> {% client.global.set("match", response.body.id); %}

### 1.3 OPS: "Plein tarif" in Est, 150 DH
POST {{base}}/org/events/{{match}}/prices
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"zone_id": {{estId}}, "name": "Plein tarif", "price_mad": 15000, "quota": 100}

> {% client.global.set("pleinCat", response.body.id); %}

### 1.4 OPS: "Tribune" in Est, 250 DH
POST {{base}}/org/events/{{match}}/prices
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"zone_id": {{estId}}, "name": "Tribune", "price_mad": 25000, "quota": 20}

> {% client.global.set("tribuneCat", response.body.id); %}

### 1.5 OPS: "Presse" in Est (Invitations, 0 DH)
POST {{base}}/org/events/{{match}}/prices
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"zone_id": {{estId}}, "name": "Presse", "price_mad": 0, "quota": 20, "audience": "INVITE"}

> {% client.global.set("presseCat", response.body.id); %}

### 1.6 OPS: publish (DRAFT -> ON_SALE)
POST {{base}}/org/events/{{match}}/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

### ---------- (2) A fan's 250 DH cash code (collected at Guichet Nord in 3.3) ----------

### 2.1 Buyer: code
POST {{base}}/fan/auth/otp
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{buyerPhone}}"}

### 2.2 Buyer: verify
POST {{base}}/fan/auth/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{buyerPhone}}", "code": "{{code}}"}

> {% client.global.set("buyerToken", response.body.token); %}

### 2.3 Buyer: one Tribune place -> 201 RESERVED
POST {{base}}/fan/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"event_id": {{match}}, "channel": "APP", "items": [{"price_category_id": "{{tribuneCat}}", "qty": 1,
  "holders": [{"name": "Omar Alaoui"}]}]}

> {% client.global.set("codeOrder", response.body.id); %}

### 2.4 Buyer: a cash code -> 200 {pay_code, amount_mad 25000}
POST {{base}}/fan/orders/{{codeOrder}}/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"method": "CASH_AGENCY"}

> {% client.global.set("payCode", response.body.pay_code); %}

### ---------- (3) Tills: Nord 3 × 150 DH + the code, declares 700 DH; Sud 2 × 150 DH, declares 300 DH ----------

### 3.1 CASHIER: open "Guichet Nord" -> 201
POST {{base}}/org/pos/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"label": "Guichet Nord"}

> {% client.global.set("nordId", response.body.id); %}

### 3.2 CASHIER: 3 places, 450 DH cash
POST {{base}}/org/pos/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"sale_id": "{{$random.uuid}}", "event_id": {{match}}, "items": [{"price_category_id": "{{pleinCat}}", "qty": 3,
  "holders": [{"name": "Yazid Aqel"}, {"name": "Yazid Aqel"}, {"name": "Yazid Aqel"}]}]}

### 3.3 CASHIER: "Encaisser" the 250 DH code -> 200, the buyer's order PAID
POST {{base}}/org/pos/codes/{{payCode}}/collect
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"amount_mad": 25000}

### 3.4 CASHIER: close declaring 700 DH -> 200 {expected_mad 70000, variance_mad 0, deposit null}
POST {{base}}/org/pos/sessions/{{nordId}}/close
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"declared_mad": 70000}

### 3.5 OPS: open "Guichet Sud" -> 201
POST {{base}}/org/pos/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"label": "Guichet Sud"}

> {% client.global.set("sudId", response.body.id); %}

### 3.6 OPS: 2 places, 300 DH cash (B3's POS 2)
POST {{base}}/org/pos/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"sale_id": "{{$random.uuid}}", "event_id": {{match}}, "items": [{"price_category_id": "{{pleinCat}}", "qty": 2,
  "holders": [{"name": "Karim Benali"}, {"name": "Karim Benali"}]}]}

### 3.7 OPS: close declaring 300 DH
POST {{base}}/org/pos/sessions/{{sudId}}/close
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"declared_mad": 30000}

### ---------- (4) B8 Encaissements and Dépôts ----------

### 4.1 FINANCE: Encaissements today -> both sessions deposit null ("Non déposé"), totals.undeposited_mad 100000
GET {{base}}/org/finance/cash?from={{today}}&to={{today}}&timezone=Africa/Casablanca
Authorization: Bearer {{financeToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

### 4.2 FINANCE: Dépôts -> undeposited lists Nord then Sud (oldest closed first)
GET {{base}}/org/finance/deposits?from={{today}}&to={{today}}
Authorization: Bearer {{financeToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

### 4.3 FINANCE: "Bordereau 448812", 990 DH over both -> 201 {declared_mad 100000, variance_mad -1000} (écart −10 DH)
# deposited_on: today, in the venue's zone (a later date is FUTURE).
POST {{base}}/org/finance/deposits
Authorization: Bearer {{financeToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"deposited_on": "{{today}}", "amount_mad": 99000, "reference": "Bordereau 448812",
 "session_ids": ["{{nordId}}", "{{sudId}}"]}

> {% client.global.set("depositId", response.body.id); %}

### 4.4 FINANCE: Guichet Sud again -> 422 VALIDATION_FAILED on session_ids[0], reason DEPOSITED ("Session déjà déposée")
POST {{base}}/org/finance/deposits
Authorization: Bearer {{financeToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"deposited_on": "{{today}}", "amount_mad": 30000, "reference": "Bordereau 448813",
 "session_ids": ["{{sudId}}"]}

### 4.5 FINANCE: Encaissements -> both sessions deposit {reference "Bordereau 448812"}, undeposited_mad 0; the CSV has depot;depose_le
GET {{base}}/org/finance/cash.csv?from={{today}}&to={{today}}&timezone=Africa/Casablanca
Authorization: Bearer {{financeToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

### ---------- (5) Void and record again ----------

### 5.1 FINANCE: void -> 403 (ADMIN only)
POST {{base}}/org/finance/deposits/{{depositId}}/void
Authorization: Bearer {{financeToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"reason": "montant mal saisi"}

### 5.2 ADMIN: void -> 200 {voided_at, voided_by, void_reason, sessions []}; both sessions "Non déposé" again
POST {{base}}/org/finance/deposits/{{depositId}}/void
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"reason": "montant mal saisi"}

### 5.3 OPS: record -> 403 (OPS reads the tab only)
POST {{base}}/org/finance/deposits
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"deposited_on": "{{today}}", "amount_mad": 100000, "reference": "Bordereau 448812",
 "session_ids": ["{{nordId}}", "{{sudId}}"]}

### 5.4 FINANCE: 1 000 DH -> 201 {variance_mad 0}
POST {{base}}/org/finance/deposits
Authorization: Bearer {{financeToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"deposited_on": "{{today}}", "amount_mad": 100000, "reference": "Bordereau 448812",
 "session_ids": ["{{nordId}}", "{{sudId}}"]}

### 5.5 OPS: Dépôts -> the live deposit and the voided one ("Annulé · montant mal saisi"); undeposited []
GET {{base}}/org/finance/deposits?from={{today}}&to={{today}}
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

### ---------- (6) B3: 3 invitations and 4 app places; channels count sales only ----------

### 6.1 OPS: 3 press invitations -> 201
POST {{base}}/org/events/{{match}}/invitations
Authorization: Bearer {{orgToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"invitation_id": "{{$random.uuid}}", "items": [{"price_category_id": "{{presseCat}}", "qty": 3, "holders": [
  {"name": "Nadia Berrada"}, {"name": "Salma Tazi"}, {"name": "Karim El Idrissi"}]}]}

### 6.2 Yazid: code
POST {{base}}/fan/auth/otp
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{yazidPhone}}"}

### 6.3 Yazid: verify
POST {{base}}/fan/auth/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{yazidPhone}}", "code": "{{code}}"}

> {% client.global.set("yazidToken", response.body.token); %}

### 6.4 Yazid: 4 places in the app -> 201
POST {{base}}/fan/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{yazidToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"event_id": {{match}}, "channel": "APP", "items": [{"price_category_id": "{{pleinCat}}", "qty": 4,
  "holders": [{"name": "Yazid Aqel"}, {"name": "Yazid Aqel"}, {"name": "Yazid Aqel"}, {"name": "Yazid Aqel"}]}]}

> {% client.global.set("yazidOrder", response.body.id); %}

### 6.5 Yazid: pay by card -> open redirect_url, "Approuver"
POST {{base}}/fan/orders/{{yazidOrder}}/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{yazidToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"method": "CARD"}

### 6.6 FINANCE: B3 -> channels APP 5 (4 + the cash-code place), POS 5 (the tills' 3 + 2), free {passes 0, invitations 3};
# paid = Σ channels.paid + free.passes + free.invitations; methods.FREE = 3
GET {{base}}/org/events/{{match}}/sales
Authorization: Bearer {{financeToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

### ---------- (7) CRM: Yazid (push), Karim (WhatsApp), Amine (nothing), Sara (joins, leaves) ----------

### 7.1 Yazid: "Yazid", fr
